      "level": 2,
      "content": "Types of Sand Dunes"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test the distinction between different sand dune types based on wind direction and sand availability.",
        "Barchans, transverse dunes, longitudinal dunes (seifs), and parabolic dunes are high-yield topics in Geography prelims and mains."
      ],
      "id": "gcgfic2"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sand dunes are prominent depositional landforms created by aeolian (wind) processes in arid and semi-arid environments.",
        "The formation and classification of sand dunes depend on factors such as wind velocity, direction, and availability of sand.",
        "Understanding dune morphology helps identify prevailing wind patterns and environmental conditions of desert regions."
      ],
      "id": "6359dzc"
    },
